# mouse_drag_window — BACKPORT to kitty v0.48.2 (2cb1d95, tag v0.48.2)
#
# Apply with:  git -C <a v0.48.2 checkout> apply docs/patches/kitty-mouse-drag-window-v0.48.2.patch
#
# This is NOT the master patch. Two hunks below exist ONLY in this file, because
# OSWindow.mouse_left_press_x/y is master-only at v0.48.2:
#   * kitty/state.h  — the field on OSWindow
#   * kitty/glfw.c   — its WRITE SITE, in the LEFT-press branch of
#                      mouse_button_callback, before the mouse_event(...) call.
# Exposing the field without the write site yields a drag armed at (0,0), which is
# indistinguishable from a successful arm in a before/after state read.
#
# Deliberately NOT ported, each for a stated reason (see
# docs/patches/kitty-mouse-drag-window-PR.md § Backport notes (v0.48.2)):
#   * kitty/shaders.c     — a DIFFERENT master-only feature that reads the same field.
#   * kitty/tabs.py        — the Q5 on_window_drop ordering fix; v0.48.2's
#                            on_window_drop is a materially different function.
#   * docs/changelog.rst   — local build, not an upstream submission.
#   * kitty_tests/*        — kitty_tests/base.py is master-only; there is no test wave.
